 employee of $647K ranks in the above the sector median among Healthcare peers. Each employee generates $167K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $25K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Waystar Holding Corp. is a mid-cap healthcare business with a $5.4B market cap on $1.1B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +17% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +9.6pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 3% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $283M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 26 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.76\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.6\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 3.1\u00d7.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 2.5% of the shares, and within its sector the business captures 2.6\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Goodwill represents 69% of total assets \u2014 a large impairment risk hanging over book value","sev":"red","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 9.0% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $8.7M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 61/100): durably derated by the market; roic below cost of capital \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 23% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading at a 36% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 13% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.7% return)"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Revenue Guidance Update Might Change Waystar Holding (WAY) Stock Narrative","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/healthcare/nasdaq-way/waystar-holding/news/revenue-guidance-update-might-change-waystar-holding-way-sto","date":"2026-11-08","timestamp":1794130040.034,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.225,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","guidance"]},{"title":"Waystar Holding (WAY) Lifts Guidance Af